    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Howley Souhan are delighted to present 3 Grosvenor Villas, Rathgar, Dublin 6, a charming three-bedroom mid-terrace home built in the 1940’s situated in this mature and highly regarded residential location. Offering well-proportioned accommodation, attractive period detailing and a private south-westerly facing rear patio type garden, this appealing home presents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to acquire a property of genuine character and create a truly special residence.\r\n\r\nThe property retains a lovely selection of original period features, including original internal doors, dado rails, picture rails and an open fireplace with tiled surround and traditional mantlepiece in the dining room. The high ceilings of approximately 2.6 metres on the ground floor further enhance the sense of space and character. Tongue-and-groove flooring has also been retained throughout the majority of the accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hall, two well-proportioned reception rooms and a galley-style kitchen. The front reception room features a modern gas fire with attractive glass façade, while the dining room enjoys the character and warmth of the original open fireplace.  On the first-floor return there is a shower room, with the first floor providing two generous double bedrooms and a single bedroom.\r\n\r\nThe location is undoubtedly one of the property's greatest attractions. Situated almost equi-distance from the centre of both Rathgar and Rathmines villages the property is tucked away in a quiet and sought-after enclave adjacent to Ashbrook Tennis Club and within walking distance of a superb range of shops, cafés, restaurants, pubs and everyday amenities within easy reach.\r\n\r\nThe property is also within easy reach of the city centre, Harold's Cross and Terenure, making it an ideal base for commuters and families alike.\r\n3 Grosvenor Villas is a fine example of a Dublin period home, combining traditional character with excellent potential, and is sure to appeal to buyers seeking a property in a well-established and highly regarded Rathgar setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor:\r\n\r\nHallway: 4.36m x 1.64m Spacious hallway with understairs storage, tongue and groove timber flooring, dado rail and picture rail.  Radiator cover.\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 4.09m x 2.93m To the front with tongue and groove timber flooring, picture rail, marble surround fireplace and hearth, and gas fire with glass façade.  \r\n\r\nDining Room: 3.9m x 3.4m To the rear with tongue and groove timber flooring and picture rail.  Original fireplace with open fire and tiled surround and hearth.  Hot press.\r\n\r\nKitchen: 2.09m x 1.7m Eye and floor level units with fridge, oven and hob.  Tiled floor, timber ceiling and door to rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Return:\r\n\r\nShower room: 2.00m x 1.96m (max) With two piece white suite and shower unit with electric shower.  Tiled floors with half tiled walls.  Window for natural light and ventilation \r\n\r\nFirst Floor:\r\n\r\nLanding: With access to attic space and dado rail.\r\n\r\nBedroom One: 3.55m x 3.38m  To the rear with tongue and groove timber flooring, picture rail and built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two: 3.00m x 2.96m To the front with tongue and groove timber flooring, picture rail, feature non-working fireplace and built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three: 2.39m x 2.05m With tongue and groove timber flooring and built in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nOutside:\r\n\r\nRear Garden:  Easily maintained rear garden with small fuel shed and timber shed with electricity for housing the washing machine, drier and freezer.\r\n\r\nFront Garden: Laid in lawn.  On-street permit parking to the front."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Approx: 78 sq.m.\r\nHighly sought after Rathgar location\r\nSituated opposite Ashbrook Tennis club\r\nSouth westerly facing rear garden\r\nGas fired radiator central heating\r\nDouble glazed windows\r\nMany original features still intact\r\nOn-street parking\r\nClose to a variety of shops, schools, recreational sports and clubs and numerous transport links.\r\nBER: D\r\nBER No: 119701415"
      },
